{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00219",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 6.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.82,
      "end_seconds": 10.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.33,
      "end_seconds": 16.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Yeah, it's pain in my right ankle. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.64,
      "end_seconds": 19.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.27,
      "end_seconds": 23.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.43,
      "end_seconds": 32.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.83,
      "end_seconds": 42.78,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "I'd give it a five, out of ten. Putting weight on it and walking definitely sets it off. It sort of comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.07,
      "end_seconds": 46.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.96,
      "end_seconds": 59.44,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get bruising as well. I've had swelling too, for five days. About swelling, I'd say severe. The bruising? That's been for one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.97,
      "end_seconds": 64.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "What about a twist during football, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.25,
      "end_seconds": 66.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Yes, since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.04,
      "end_seconds": 71.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Have you had any pain in the knee or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.69,
      "end_seconds": 76.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "No pain in the knee or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.19,
      "end_seconds": 81.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Any numbness, pain at the back of the heel or pop or crack?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.59,
      "end_seconds": 84.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.19,
      "end_seconds": 88.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Right, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.8,
      "end_seconds": 90.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.88,
      "end_seconds": 95.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Alright, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.79,
      "end_seconds": 98.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.5,
      "end_seconds": 102.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.64,
      "end_seconds": 107.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "So, my mother has diabetes. My uncle had colon cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.57,
      "end_seconds": 114.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.43,
      "end_seconds": 125.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, uh, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.89,
      "end_seconds": 127.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.89,
      "end_seconds": 128.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.69,
      "end_seconds": 132.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.13,
      "end_seconds": 138.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had heart failure for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.53,
      "end_seconds": 140.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.59,
      "end_seconds": 144.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Yes, an underactive thyroid. High blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.02,
      "end_seconds": 153.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.14,
      "end_seconds": 155.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.26,
      "end_seconds": 158.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.89,
      "end_seconds": 163.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "So, it's furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning for the fluid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 164.13,
      "end_seconds": 168.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 80 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.38,
      "end_seconds": 175.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.56,
      "end_seconds": 203.24,
      "duration_seconds": 24.68,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. It's thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. Ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. Right, I take Volini spray, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 203.76,
      "end_seconds": 212.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 124 over 73, temperature is 36.7 degrees, pulse is 64 beats a minute, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.4,
      "end_seconds": 214.1,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.18,
      "end_seconds": 220.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.91,
      "end_seconds": 222.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.7,
      "end_seconds": 226.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.12,
      "end_seconds": 244.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "The bones themselves aren't tender and the ankle feels stable when I test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.77,
      "end_seconds": 248.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.44,
      "end_seconds": 261.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle, tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.1,
      "end_seconds": 265.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.41,
      "end_seconds": 283.46,
      "duration_seconds": 14.05,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.54,
      "end_seconds": 297.8,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.37,
      "end_seconds": 320.68,
      "duration_seconds": 21.31,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with an ankle sprain at this stage. It could also be a ligament tear, so we'll keep that open. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your right ankle for about two weeks, and no pop or crack or pain at the back of the heel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.71,
      "end_seconds": 323.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 324.38,
      "end_seconds": 328.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I've already done an X-ray of the ankle, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.48,
      "end_seconds": 343.21,
      "duration_seconds": 13.73,
      "text": "Okay, thanks, I'll look at that. I'd like you to take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for ankle pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.88,
      "end_seconds": 346.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.17,
      "end_seconds": 366.63,
      "duration_seconds": 18.46,
      "text": "Rest, ice for twenty minutes at a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.07,
      "end_seconds": 368.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.65,
      "end_seconds": 375.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.28,
      "end_seconds": 376.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.91,
      "end_seconds": 381.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.7,
      "end_seconds": 382.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.87,
      "end_seconds": 385.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.02,
      "end_seconds": 388.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    }
  ]
}